  MUST contain actual generated field values, NOT empty `{}` or dicts with only comments inside.
- **NEVER use bare `pass` statements** that leave variables uninitialized. If you have conditional
  branches (if/elif/else) that build a `data` dict, EVERY branch must assign to `data`:
  ```python
  # WRONG - causes UnboundLocalError when payment_type is "crypto"
  if payment_type == "credit_card":
      data = {...}
  elif payment_type == "crypto":
      pass  # NO! This leaves `data` undefined!

  # CORRECT - all branches assign to `data`
  if payment_type == "credit_card":
      data = {"payment_type": "credit_card", "card_number": ...}
  elif payment_type == "crypto":
      data = {"payment_type": "crypto", "wallet_address": ...}  # Must define all fields!
  ```
- **NEVER copy example comments from this prompt** - generate real functional code, not examples

